
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <base href="/" />
    <ResourcePreloader />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["lib/bootstrap/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css"]" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["app.css"]" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["AeroGrid.WebDashboard.styles.css"]" />
    <ImportMap />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="favicon.png" />
    <HeadOutlet />
</head>

<body>
    @* MODIFIED BY AI (critical fix): added @@rendermode="InteractiveServer" below.
       Program.cs already registers interactive server components
       (AddInteractiveServerComponents / AddInteractiveServerRenderMode), but that only makes
       the capability available -- nothing in the component tree was actually opting into it.
       Without this attribute, every page (including GridManager) rendered as static HTML
       only: the initial page load's data was real (OnInitializedAsync still runs once during
       static prerendering, which is why the first weather fetch for the default city worked),
       but no further interaction could ever reach the server afterward -- typing into the
       city box and clicking "Sync Live Grid" were both inert, since two-way data binding and
       click handlers require a live interactive circuit to do anything. This is also why
       toggling an asset appeared to do nothing: the checkbox click never reached the server
       either. This was a pre-existing gap in the project (App.razor/Routes.razor were not
       files touched by any earlier change here), not something introduced by any of the other
       Sprint 6 work -- but it's what was actually blocking both the weather search AND the
       asset toggle from ever responding to input at all.
       (This explanation is a Razor comment, not an HTML comment, specifically so the @ symbols
       above are never mistaken for real Razor syntax by the compiler.) *@
    <Routes @rendermode="InteractiveServer" />
    <ReconnectModal />
    <script src="@Assets["_framework/blazor.web.js"]"></script>
</body>

</html>
